solve?\r\n\r\nCorrect the documentation's explanation of the smoothing curve. For non-empty ranges, the interpolation is slowest at the beginning and end of the range, and fastest halfway through.\r\nAlign the C# return behavior when the range is empty (`from == to`) with Godot Core / GDScript.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThe documentation is based on the existing Core / GDScript documentation:\r\n[doc/classes/@GlobalScope.xml](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/doc/classes/%40GlobalScope.xml)\r\n\r\nThe C# implementation now matches the existing Core behavior:\r\n[core/math/math_funcs.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/math/math_funcs.h)\r\n\r\n## Testing \r\nBuilt Godot with C# support and compiled GodotSharp.\r\nRan a local C# runtime test covering the float and double empty-range cases, positive and negative ranges. All checks passed.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/u